\name{cellucid_cells_open}
\alias{cellucid_cells_open}
\title{Open a share of the cells}
\usage{
cellucid_cells_open(
  viewer,
  mode,
  allocation = "proportional",
  count,
  embedding,
  field,
  fraction,
  method = NULL,
  seed = NULL
)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{mode}{all: every cell; subsample: the count or fraction given. One of \code{"all"}, \code{"subsample"}. Required.}
\item{allocation}{Stratified: how the cells are split over the categories. One of \code{"proportional"}, \code{"balanced"}. Default \code{"proportional"}, the viewer's own.}
\item{count}{How many cells, exactly (at least 2; the dataset's count or more opens every cell). Not with fraction. A whole number (at least 1). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{embedding}{Spatial: the obsm embedding it thins. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{field}{Stratified: the categorical column it is stratified by. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{fraction}{The share of the dataset's cells: 0.1 opens a tenth, 1 every cell. Not with count. A number (more than 0, at most 1). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{method}{How the cells are chosen; null for the file's default. One of \code{"uniform"}, \code{"blocks"}, \code{"stratified"}, \code{"spatial"}, \code{NULL}. Default \code{NULL}, the viewer's own.}
\item{seed}{The subsample's seed; null for the file's. A whole number or \code{NULL} (at least 0, at most 4294967295). Default \code{NULL}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Read the dataset again with every cell, or with a subsample: an exact \code{count} of cells or a \code{fraction} of them, chosen by a subsample method; highlights, labels, views and filters are kept for the cells still open.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{cells.open} (Data). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{cells}, \code{mapping}, \code{expression}, \code{field-overlays}, \code{gene-sets}, \code{views}, \code{active-field}, \code{filters}, \code{colors}, \code{visibility}, \code{highlights}, \code{camera}, \code{settings}, \code{analysis}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_cells_open(viewer, mode = "all")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
